@@ -0,0 +1,147 @@
+# Public-information positioning for checkpoint 25,772
+
+## Accelerated battle scoring
+
+The native backend takes a batch of candidate boards, opponent boards, and
+explicit seeds in one Rust call. It reproduces the pinned v30 combat priority,
+NumPy MT19937 draws, supported abilities, perks, and post-removal summons.
+Unrepresented abilities, copied abilities, and bounded fights that need
+reference resolution go to the Python simulator with their original seeds.
+Native and reference results are combined in the original candidate order.
+The shop, action legality, policy, optimizer, and learning rule stay in Python.
+
+The accelerated planner also reuses the public history shared by its eight
+opponent hypotheses, isolates mutable player state for each friendly order,
+and uses CUDA graphs for repeated FP32 inference. An eager path is available
+when graph capture is unsupported. The training protocol records the native
+binary and source hashes. The native library checks the Python mechanics
+source hashes before accepting boards.
+
+Run the complete-update comparison from the SAP workspace on an available GPU slot.
+
+```bash
+release_dir=/absolute/path/to/restored-release
+planner_dir=$(realpath sapai-gym/research/public_planner)
+study_dir=$(realpath sapai-gym/research/selfplay)
+result_dir=$(mktemp -d)
+lib=$(bash "$planner_dir/build_battle.sh" "$result_dir/native")
+docker run --rm --network none --gpus all --cpus 4 --memory 12g --memory-swap 12g \
+  --user "$(id -u):$(id -g)" -e OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 -e OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 \
+  -e MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 -e TORCH_ALLOW_TF32_CUBLAS_OVERRIDE=0 \
+  -e PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \
+  -e SAP_BATTLE_LIBRARY="/results/native/$(basename "$lib")" \
+  -e PYTHONPATH=/study:/planner:/workspace/runs/claude-end-positioner-20261112-v1 \
+  -v "$release_dir:/workspace:ro" -v "$planner_dir:/planner:ro" \
+  -v "$study_dir:/study:ro" -v "$result_dir:/results" \
+  --entrypoint python sap-rl-shared:research-25772 /study/bench_prepared_update.py \
+  --backends original native --rollout-width 64 --output /results/benchmark
+```
+
+Each world block trains both shoppers on 512 decisions each. The benchmark
+reverses backend order on block two and compares collected turns, both-seat
+actions and reorders, selected batches, policy weights, and optimizer state.
+Read `secondsPerThousand` and `speedup` in `benchmark/result.json`.
+The same release mounts support `check_native_scorer.py --out REPORT` for
+seeded differential testing and `check_fast_planner.py --output REPORT`
+for opponent-shop trace comparisons. Supply a writable report path.
+
+`PublicOpponentPlanner` wraps the released policy at end of turn. It rebuilds
+an opponent shop from the last revealed board, scoreboard and round result,
+using an independent shop tape and zero opponent memory. It simulates eight
+opponent turns, scores reachable friendly team orders with seeded battles,
+and lets the policy play its regular shop decisions. Unknown shop modifiers
+start at their defaults. The reconstruction treats visible effective stats as
+permanent, so expiring buffs can cause a forecast error.
+
+The earlier simulated-opponent planner cloned the live opponent before
+rerolling its shop. Changing only a hidden +2 shop bonus changed its predicted
+pet stats while the acting player's observation stayed identical. This folder
+contains the replacement used for the fresh evaluation.
+
+## Evidence
+
+With the frozen v30 simulator and identical update-25,772 weights on both
+sides, the planner won **73 of 128** complete matches. Each of 64 fresh seeds
+was played from both seats. The planner won both on 13 seeds, split 47 pairs
+and lost both on four. The mean match score was 57.03%, with a seat-paired
+bootstrap 95% interval of 50.78% to 63.28%. This is a mirror-policy
+comparison. Strength against top human players is unmeasured.
+
+Against two historical opponents, the planner's mirror advantage did not
+transfer. Each row below uses 32 fresh seeds, with both policies playing
+both seats against the same frozen opponent.
+
+| Opponent | Raw 25,772 | Planner | Paired score change (95% bootstrap interval) |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| v22 update 2,000 | 50–14 | 49–15 | −1.6 pp [−14.1, +9.4] |
+| v25 update 300 | 52–12 | 52–12 | 0.0 pp [−10.9, +10.9] |
+
+The equally weighted change across opponents was −0.8 percentage points
+[−9.4, +7.8], resampling whole world seeds across both opponents together.
+Use raw 25,772 as the baseline. The planner remains a research candidate
+with a demonstrated advantage in its mirror matchup. The [paired game
+scores and configurations](benchmark.json) cover all 384 matches.
+
+## Run from a restored release
+
+Restore the release assets using the [workspace instructions](../README.md).
+Use the copy of this folder from the checkout containing this guide, and the
+Docker image built from the restored release. The example starts with one
+complete seat pair and saves a result after each game.
+
+```bash
+release_dir=/absolute/path/to/restored-release
+planner_dir=/absolute/path/to/sapai-gym/research/public_planner
+results=$(mktemp -d)
+docker run --rm --network none --gpus all --cpus 4 --memory 8g \
+  --user "$(id -u):$(id -g)" -e OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 -e OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 \
+  -e TORCH_ALLOW_TF32_CUBLAS_OVERRIDE=0 -e PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \
+  -e PYTHONPATH=/workspace/runs/claude-end-positioner-20261112-v1 \
+  -e SAP_PANEL_OUTPUT=/results -v "$release_dir:/workspace:ro" \
+  -v "$planner_dir:/planner:ro" -v "$results:/results" -w /results \
+  --entrypoint python sap-rl-shared /planner/public_panel.py --start 0 --stop 1
+```
+
+For the full fixed panel, change `--stop 1` to `--stop 64` and reuse the
+same output directory. Then use `--summary` with the same mounts to
+calculate the paired interval. Keep a separate results directory for
+each source version. The actor loader checks the checkpoint SHA-256 and
+the frozen reference bootstrap verifies the simulator source.
+
+To exercise the information boundary on CPU, replace the final script
+and arguments with `/planner/check_public_position.py` and omit `--gpus all`.
+The check compares candidate boards, predicted opponent boards, battle
+scores and selected moves on two public positions after varying private
+opponent state and future randomness.
+
+## Operator-run human matches
+
+For a local practice match, use the restored release, choose seat 0 or 1,
+and supply a directory for result receipts. Human matches default to raw
+25,772. To evaluate the corrected positioner, set `SAP_MATCH_MODE=planner`
+before creating the series and keep it set for play. The precommitted plan
+and every game receipt record the policy mode.
+
+```bash
+bash "$planner_dir/run_matched_play.sh" "$release_dir" 0 ./practice-receipts
+```
+
+For a held-out series, agree on the eligibility criteria and roster first.
+Prepare a JSON array containing a `player` identifier and a `qualification`
+reference for each entrant. The following commands create the schedule, run
+one scheduled match, and read the score. Keep the printed digest before
+playing. The schedule balances seats within each player and the scorer
+reports unstarted or interrupted attempts. Players' moves are not used
+for training.
+
+```bash
+digest=$(python3 "$planner_dir/heldout_series.py" create ./series \
+  --roster roster.json --games-per-player 4 --release "$release_dir")
+python3 "$planner_dir/heldout_series.py" play ./series "$digest" \
+  --player "ROSTER_ID" --release "$release_dir"
+python3 "$planner_dir/heldout_series.py" score ./series "$digest"
+```
+
+Four games per player illustrates the command syntax. Series size and
+qualification evidence must suit the claim being tested. Set
+`SAP_MATCH_IMAGE` if the locally built Docker image has a different tag.
