@@ -0,0 +1,109 @@
+# Self-play loop
+
+Start from a restored update-25,772 release and the runtime described in the
+[release guide](../README.md). From the SAP workspace:
+
+```bash
+bash sapai-gym/research/selfplay/run.sh /absolute/path/to/restored-release \
+    "$PWD/runs/league-continuation-25772-v2"
+docker logs -f sap-loop-league-continuation-25772-v2
+```
+
+Read the last learner update, decisions trained, completed match evaluations,
+and current champion from the host:
+
+```bash
+python3 sapai-gym/research/selfplay/status.py runs/league-continuation-25772-v2
+```
+
+For the longer opponent-pool league, use the same command with its run directory.
+
+```bash
+python3 sapai-gym/research/selfplay/status.py runs/population-league-25772-v1
+```
+
+It reports the latest learner update, the most recent saved checkpoint,
+and completed match panels as their receipts appear. The population run
+collects updates 384 and 1,024 before evaluating them on common worlds.
+
+Set `SAP_MATCH_IMAGE` to your local image tag if it differs from
+`sap-rl-shared:research-25772`. Repeating the command detects a live run.
+If the container exited, it can restart the same experiment. The controller
+verifies the last completed milestone and repeats an incomplete stage in a
+new attempt directory. It keeps failed attempts for diagnosis.
+
+The learner trains against mirrors of its evolving policy and a pool of
+frozen opponents. The native league sampler uses past match outcomes to
+weight residents. Self-play begins with 25,772's weights, a fresh optimizer,
+and an empty match history. Subsequent milestones restore the learner,
+optimizer, and league. The run uses four CPU cores and caps the learner's
+CUDA allocator at 6 GiB; Docker host memory has a separate 12 GiB cap.
+
+At updates 16, 128, and 384, the candidate plays 32 seat-swapped monitoring
+seeds against raw 25,772. If it scores above 50%, it also plays 64 fresh
+seed pairs against the current champion. Promotion requires the one-sided
+paired bootstrap lower bound to exceed 50%, with a nominal error allowance
+of 0.05/3 per milestone. This identifies a league champion under these
+conditions. A claim about broader playing strength requires further opponents.
+
+The run directory contains:
+
+- `stage-*/training.log` for live learner updates and league sampling.
+- `trained-*.json` for verified checkpoint paths, hashes, and accepted decisions.
+- `score-*.json` for terminal match scores, seeds, and seats.
+- `progression.json` for the incumbent and completed milestones.
+
+The bounded run ends after update 384. The [research objective](RESEARCH_GOAL.md)
+sets the decision for the following cycle based on those results.
+
+## Positioning during training
+
+The separate `position_trial.py` experiment starts two shoppers from the
+same released policy. One receives the corrected public planner's reorder
+at its own END. The other executes its sampled END directly. Both keep
+their normal buy, sell, roll, and MOVE actions. Planner moves contribute
+to the board that fights; the learner records only its own decisions and
+their behavior probabilities.
+
+Each update uses the same collection worlds, seats and opponent assignments
+for both arms. A length-only selection of complete turns gives each optimizer
+exactly 512 decisions. `training.json` distinguishes collected data from
+trained decisions and counts selected purchase turns that actually received
+a reorder. The pilot runs 32 updates and saves both models and optimizers
+atomically in `training.pt` after each update. Assessment uses fresh paired
+matches between the frozen shoppers with the same public planner on both
+sides, then with both shoppers playing unaided. A single pilot training
+seed gives preliminary evidence.
+
+On an available GPU slot, use a new output directory (or the same
+directory to resume a matching protocol):
+
+```bash
+bash sapai-gym/research/selfplay/run_position_trial.sh /absolute/path/to/restored-release \
+    "$PWD/runs/position-trial-25772-v1"
+```
+
+For a new run choose a fresh directory. The launcher snapshots the method,
+builds the batched Rust scorer with the host Rust compiler, and records the
+selected backend and binary hash in `protocol.json`. A machine without
+a Rust compiler uses the compact Python scorer. `SAP_SCORER=native` requires
+the native build, `SAP_SCORER=compact` selects Python battle scoring, and
+`SAP_SCORER=reference` selects the original planner and scorer.
+
+New accelerated training runs evaluate all eight simulated opponents in a
+width-8 batch. `SAP_ROLLOUT_WIDTH=64` preserves the released actor's original
+FP32 computation shape. A different batch shape can affect
+FP32 rounding. Both settings retain the configured search budget. The
+launcher records the chosen width and reuses it on resume.
+
+The narrower native configuration can be selected with the following command.
+
+```bash
+SAP_SCORER=native SAP_ROLLOUT_WIDTH=8 \
+  bash sapai-gym/research/selfplay/run_position_trial.sh /absolute/path/to/restored-release \
+  "$PWD/runs/position-trial-native"
+```
+
+The [scorer guide](../public_planner/README.md) includes the build and
+complete-update benchmark. Existing completed runs can still be inspected
+with their original receipts.
