@@ -0,0 +1,386 @@
+# Autonomous SAP self-play research
+
+Pursue superhuman Turtle Pack 1v1 play starting from checkpoint 25,772. Keep
+the self-play league working and autonomously choose, run, and evaluate the
+next credible experiment. Use public observations, matched rules, and
+simulator outcomes. Human matches are reserved for final validation. Continue
+AI research while human players are unavailable. Use no new human strategy
+labels, demonstrations, or coaching.
+
+Track whole-match playing strength. Report checkpoint, decisions trained,
+opponents, seat-swapped match score, uncertainty, and promotion decision.
+Measure against a fixed baseline and periodically against diverse frozen
+opponents. Confirm a promising candidate on unused seeds before promotion.
+Reserve the superhuman claim for a held-out top-human benchmark after strong
+and repeatable AI results.
+
+At each continuation, inspect actual jobs, checkpoints, and completed results.
+Monitor a healthy job. Diagnose failures and resume from a verified checkpoint.
+When a run finishes, choose the next bounded training or research cycle based
+on the evidence and launch it if it fits the shared machine's existing resource
+limits. When results stall, test a materially different explanation. Preserve
+failed trials and the last confirmed champion. Report consequential findings
+and ask for input when further work needs new authority or external resources.
+
+## Current run
+
+The completed ordinary league directory is `sap-rl/runs/league-continuation-25772-v2`.
+The controller starts from the released model's weights with fresh optimizer
+and league state. It uses current-policy mirrors, a frozen starting policy,
+and rolling historical checkpoints. Later stages restore the learner's
+optimizer and league. The three evaluation milestones are 16, 128, and 384
+new updates. Each uses full-match scores against 25,772; promising candidates
+also face the current champion on separate seeds. Check `progression.json`
+and the stage logs when continuing research. A completed bounded run is a
+decision point for the next experiment.
+
+The controller and final cross-play check exited successfully. Update 384
+trained on 1,655,547 decisions and scored 60–68 against 25,772 on independent
+confirmation. Its paired score change relative to 25,772 averaged −2.34
+percentage points across v22 and v25, with a bootstrap interval of −10.94 to
++6.25. See `crossplay/summary.json` in the run directory. Retain 25,772.
+
+## Next training question: does positioning change what the agent learns to buy?
+
+The previous planner comparisons enabled search at evaluation on fixed weights.
+They leave open whether a shopper undervalues a purchase because its own later
+positioning is weak. Preserve the current unassisted cycle as a reference.
+Prioritize a matched training experiment from one checkpoint: ordinary self-play
+and self-play with the corrected public positioner on the learner's own END.
+Keep shop choices learned, draw scenarios from self-play, and measure terminal
+match results on fresh seeds against multiple opponents. Do not select particular
+pets or label strategies from human examples.
+
+Before a long run, verify that an assisted END is a legal environment transition
+and that policy-gradient records contain only decisions sampled by the learner,
+with their true behavior probabilities. Let buys receive the resulting rewards.
+Compare both trained shoppers under the same positioner at evaluation, and also
+with assistance off, to distinguish learned improvements from help at play time.
+Record extra search cost and match the training decision budgets.
+
+The first matched pilot is `position_trial.py`. It starts both arms at
+25,772, uses 32 updates of exactly 512 learned decisions per arm, and selects
+complete shop turns by length with an outcome-independent shuffle. The two
+arms face the same schedule of world seeds, seats, and frozen-within-update
+opponents. The public positioner intervenes only on the assisted shopper's
+sampled END. Its moves are environmental actions, not imitation targets.
+The two frozen trained policies then play each other on 32 new seed pairs
+with assistance for both, and on the same pairs with assistance off for both.
+
+The CPU launch/resume check passed in `runs/position-trial-contract-v1`.
+The full pilot was launched in `runs/position-trial-25772-v1` after that check,
+the league run, and the cycle-end cross-play check succeeded. It uses the
+existing shared GPU limits and saves both optimizers after each matched
+update. Check the real processes and `training.json` before resuming.
+16,384 decisions per arm and one training seed are a pilot learning point.
+Use actual cost, effect size and uncertainty to choose whether to scale or
+replicate it; a tie at this scale does not settle the purchase-credit question.
+
+Both arms completed the planned 16,384 decisions. The frozen head-to-head
+evaluation is in the same trial directory. A separate CPU screen at
+`runs/position-trial-raw-transfer-96-v1` compares both frozen shoppers and
+the original parent without search against the parent, v22, and v25. All
+three arms use the same 96 new world seeds and swap seats. Summarize the
